// M18 Phase 1: a cell-based creature (research/m18-creature-biology.md).
// `kind: Creature` -- never moves via the CA sweep, exactly like `Plant`;
// relocated explicitly by the M18 active-site scheduler (`creature.rs`),
// which reads/writes it through the ordinary `World::get`/`set`.
//
// Flammable with real numbers, same treatment fire.rs already gives every
// other material kind uniformly -- this is the entire mechanism behind "a
// worm dies to fire", no creature-specific code needed for it at all.
// `ignition_temperature` is left unset (never spontaneously ignites from
// nearby heat alone): the worm's own thermotaxis (creature.rs) is what
// handles "near a fire" by fleeing before contact; only direct contact with
// a burning neighbour (flammability) should actually catch it alight,
// mirroring how a real animal that fails to flee in time gets burned.
// `density` doesn't drive movement for a Creature cell the way it does for
// a Powder (creature.rs never displaces via the CA sweep), but the field is
// still required and set to a plausible soft-tissue value.
(
    name: "worm",
    display: "Worm",
    kind: Creature,
    density: 1.0,
    colors: [
        (176, 92, 88),
        (166, 82, 78),
        (186, 102, 96),
    ],
    flammability: 0.6,
    burn_temperature: 500.0,
    burn_duration: 60,
    burns_into: "corpse",
    heat_conductivity: 0.1,

    // **Live flesh, on the same footing as every other animal in the world.**
    // Like `beetle.ron` this authored neither field until 2026-09-02 and
    // defaulted to 0.0, so nothing could eat a living worm at any gut bias --
    // `Reports/creature-genome-flexibility-2026-09-02.md` 11a (P1).
    //
    // **480 is the world's flesh price, and unlike the beetle's it is not a
    // derivation, because there is nothing to derive it from.** The
    // flesh-pricing invariant pins `food_energy` to the species'
    // `body_energy`; `worm.ron`'s species file declares no `creature:` block
    // at all -- the worm is the pre-`CreatureDef` hardcoded animal, run by
    // `creature.rs`'s `WORM_*` constants -- so it has no `body_energy` to pin
    // to, and `creature_dies` reads 0.0 for it. 480 is what `ant`, `ancestor`,
    // `corpse` and all four `chitin`/`ant_*` materials carry, so it is the one
    // rule that generalises rather than a number chosen for this file.
    //
    // **What that costs, stated rather than hidden:** the ledger cannot see
    // it. A worm is granted `WORM_START_ENERGY` by `plant_worm_seed` with no
    // `EnergyLedger::granted` booking and no stamp, so worm flesh eaten is
    // energy the ledger never sourced. This widens a hole rather than opening
    // one -- the worm has been outside the ledger since it was written -- and
    // it closes for free the day the worm moves onto a `CreatureDef` like
    // every other species, at which point this number wants re-deriving from
    // whatever `body_energy` that file authors.
    food_energy: 480.0,
    // In MPa like every other value of this field. **Soft-bodied, and softer
    // than the 0.25 of insect cuticle** -- a worm has no shell to get
    // through. Under the weakest shipped bite (0.3), so everything with a
    // mouth can eat one.
    penetration_resistance: 0.15,
    food_class: 1.0,
)
